From be044470cae96a98344191f52df0639d63947099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:41:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] agents.resume: keep a resumable child's run under the
 session's cache root

A child that keeps its own session (agents.childSession) was still
resumable only while its run directory survived: resumable runs lived
in a managed temporary root, which is deleted when the session closes
(or on a reboot that clears the temp directory), and a new host had no
handle for a run an earlier host settled.

With this setting enabled, a Pi session's run root now lives under the
user cache directory keyed by the Pi session id, so continuing the same
session adopts its settled runs and re-executes only the launch
resume.json recorded. A run whose host died before it settled is adopted
as an interrupted attempt once that host process and the child pid it
last launched are gone and the run has stopped writing. Retention gains
retention.resumableRunMs (seven days) and the UI/settings, docs and
tests cover the new window and adoption rules.
