 - `durableWorkerRecovery` (default `false`): let a restarted resident host re-attach, or relaunch on its journal, an unfinished `pi-durable` run launched with `residency: "durable"` on the `process` transport. A run it cannot recover settles with `outcome: "indeterminate"`. See [durable-pi.md](durable-pi.md#opt-in-reattach-after-a-resident-host-restart).
 - `durableWorkerSession` (default `false`): give a `pi-durable` child without a seeded session a private Pi session file in its run directory, and put a worker-role entry at the root of its session (fork and handoff seeds too). A relaunch then keeps what extensions saved in the session. With it off, the child runs with `--no-session` as before. See [durable-pi.md](durable-pi.md#opt-in-a-session-file-for-pi-durable-workers).
-- `childSession` (default `false`): give every Pi child a private Pi session file inside its run directory (a seeded child already runs inside its seed), so a child that stopped, failed, timed out, or finished can be continued from its own transcript with [`agents.resume`](agents.md#resume-a-child-from-its-own-transcript). The host writes the file and records the exact launch beside it as the only thing a resume may re-execute. A run launched while this setting was off has no resume record, and `agents.resume` says so. Children still keep no session in Pi's own store, so trackers see them only through `sessionExport`.
+- `childSession` (default `false`): give every Pi child a private Pi session file inside its run directory (a seeded child already runs inside its seed), so a child that stopped, failed, timed out, or finished can be continued from its own transcript with [`agents.resume`](agents.md#resume-a-child-from-its-own-transcript). The host writes the file and records the exact launch beside it as the only thing a resume may re-execute. A run launched while this setting was off has no resume record, and `agents.resume` says so. Children still keep no session in Pi's own store, so trackers see them only through `sessionExport`. Because a resumable run must survive the host that launched it, enabling this setting moves the session's run root out of the temporary directory and into the user cache directory: `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/pi-fabric/runs/<pi-session-id>` (`~/.cache` by default, `PI_FABRIC_RESUME_ROOT` overrides the base). Continuing that same Pi session — after a crash, a reboot, or a plain `pi -c` — finds the settled runs again and `agents.resume` adopts them. A different session id never sees them. `retention.resumableRunMs` bounds how long they stay.
 - `notifyOnComplete`: show concise detached `agents.spawn()` completion notices and batch unread results for Main at a safe tool-turn boundary (or wake idle Main). `wait`/`join` and terminal `status` retract pending notifications; running/UI status does not. Escape/error parks results until new input.
 - `sessionExport`: export each agent run's usage as an attributed pi-format session file (on by default).
 - `sessionExportDir`: override the export store root (default `~/.pi-fabric/agent`, with `PI_FABRIC_AGENT_DIR` taking precedence).
